-- title:
--   From HTo G Move Right Left Term
-- statement:
--   **First move-right identity for the left action.** For arbitrary operators $U$, $T$, and $S$ on the local index space, the product with a left-placed $U$ can be moved through the right placement without changing the right factor:
--
--   $$
--   \left(L(UTT^{\mathsf H})R(S)\right)L(U)=L(UTT^{\mathsf H}U)R(S).
--   $$
--
--   Here $L(A)=A\otimes I$ and $R(B)=I\otimes B$. The identity is pure tensor-placement and operator-associativity algebra; it does not require positivity, normalization, or commutativity assumptions. It is the local algebra step used by `fromHToGAdjacentStageA0_pointwise_leftShape` to convert the filtered pointwise sum into the left-action target shape.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_moveRight_left_term`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
